{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies","id":1019375,"title":"Pure Breed and Black Furies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-19T12:53:19-08:00","id":1019375,"title":"Pure Breed and Black Furies","content":"How does Pure Breed work for male Garou born to the Black Furies? Do they lose it when they are accepted by Unicorn?<br /> <br /> Do their Garou Daughters return to the Black Furies gain the benefits of their CoG Father's Pure Breed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-19-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T14:22:57-08:00","id":1019422,"title":"","content":"The books are kind of contradictory on Pure Breed. So the best way to handle these things depends highly on how you interpret what the Trait really represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:37:59-08:00","id":1019513,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed seems to be spiritual in the sense it is specific to each tribe. It doesn't carry if the Garou somehow becomes a member of a different tribe that his lineage indicates.<br /> <br /> The answer to the first question is a strong &quot;yes&quot;. Male Black Fury don't get the Pure Breed rating their sister gets after becoming a Black Fury.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there is much official guidance on the second question, and it depends on how you view it. On a &quot;genetic&quot; level, such a daughter should retain at least some Pure Breed. However, if there is a strong spiritual component, it is possible that the father's admittance into another tribe might &quot;pollute&quot; that pure breed and deny the daughter any benefit of Pure Breed. Different STs probably have different positions. For me, given the relative rarity of Pure Breed, I'd probably rule it wouldn't happen - but if a PC had that as a concept and really wanted it, I wouldn't argue about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:50:19-08:00","id":1019524,"title":"","content":"I think it said somewhere, that they kept an eye on the children of wayward children who joined the CoG to invite their daughters to join the tribe<br /> <br /> so I'd say yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T23:40:57-08:00","id":1019634,"title":"","content":"They keep the black and white coat and greek features, but lose the spiritual benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:45:04-08:00","id":1019878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1019634#post1019634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They keep the black and white coat and greek features, but lose the spiritual benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Human ethnicity got removed from consideration in W20, though. It was just consistent tribal membership through generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:47:39-08:00","id":1019881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1019878#post1019878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Human ethnicity got removed from consideration in W20, though. It was just consistent tribal membership through generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, just tried to be broad with editions here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T01:39:57-08:00","id":1020227,"title":"","content":"I go by something that was written by Ethan Skemp (developer) on the old White Wolf forums and kind of is in the books as well: <b>Pure Breed is tribe specific.</b><br /> <br /> So, while a male Black Furie can have the trait in theory at birth, we usually don't build characters with stats for right after the start breathing, but when they are adults, or at least pre-change teenagers. By that time the cub can't be the paragon of being a black fury because, without the upbringing and education and acceptance by the tribe, this position is not his. Therefore the trait representing this position should be zero.<br /> The Rite of Passage includes the person into another tribe, and while the person can strive to be a paragon of the tribe, the additional kick from having this position inherited is not possible. The same goes for the Rite of Adoption. If one changes the tribe pure breed is lost.<br /> <br /> There are of course some exceptions, I'd allow. If someone like Albrecht is basically banished and doesn't work on being a paragon of his tribe and garou-kind, the pure breed still isn't lost, for his heritage is still there for the taking. I'd also allow for a mixed-tribe child (from kin/garou parings or metis-born) to be pure bred for one of the parents tribes (even the kin parents), if this is the tribe of the child, too.<br /> <br /> Surely, it would make things easier if Pure Breed made one a paragon of garou-kind and was not tribal specific, but that's not how it is inteded according to the then-werewolf-developer. And I rather like the idea, that if you have pure breed, I as the ST can tell you, that you are supposed to be more archetypical of the tribe you play, then other characters. For, I love archtypes in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T20:03:56-08:00","id":1020765,"title":"","content":"How does that relate to Pure Breed in Kinfolk though? Do Human Kinfolk lose their Pure Breed Background if they marry into another Tribe? Do Wolf Kinfolk lose their Pure Breed Background if they join a pack of another Tribe?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T22:14:53-08:00","id":1020777,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed in kinfolk is more like &quot;what spiritual breed benefit can this kinfolk give to his Garou descendants&quot; and not an actual trait they can use. Because kinfolk aren't tribe members (they never go through a rite of baptism to be accepted by a totem), they don't lose anything if they mate with a Garou from a different tribe. But I would say their descendants only get that potential Pure Breed if they go with the right tribe. If they go with another tribe, their lineage doesn't help them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T08:10:16-08:00","id":1021574,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I have never really understood the Pure Breed trait as a physical thing unless you are the product of years of incest. In my mind, it has to be a spiritual only thing, in which case you could definitely possess it, regardless of the tribe. Maybe you have the regal bearing of an ancient foe, maybe your aura is pure like the Wyrm slayers of old, or perhaps your voice carries in it the weight of ages of singers who came before you. All in all, I find it to be fairly useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T10:34:31-08:00","id":1021615,"title":"","content":"Regardless of how one interprets the nature of Pure Breed, it's one of the best investments for social/political focused Garou. Up to +5 dice to all your social rolls with other Garou is kind of insane (esp. since it applies to facedowns).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:53:47-08:00","id":1021654,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed is a physical thing that is often referred to as almost mystical (Revised, p. 122). The social dice pool bonus is one of the reasons why the Silver Fangs (which traditionally had to have three levels of Pure Breed) tended to rule the Garou Nation. I am curious though, would you say that the social dice pool bonus from Garou Pure Breed should apply to interactions with Garou Kinfolk? I would imagine that would allow Garou with high levels of Pure Breed to seduce Garou Kinfolk more easily, which would lead to greater reproductive success. In addition, it would seem that Garou Kinfolk receive their reproductive bonuses in addition to the social bonuses that they would receive when interacting with Garou (Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, p. 51).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:52:28-08:00","id":1021673,"title":"","content":"So quick Pure Breed question...that bonus applies to gifts that require a social die pool like &quot;Strength of Will&quot; or &quot;Mastery&quot; correct? I always played it that way because I never spotted a rule that said it didn't apply. Because if I've been playing it right, I think that helps highlight just how useful pure breed is to a Garou (especially considering the Garou unlike the other Fera have a relatively large number of fallen members to fight and use these dice pools in offensive gifts like &quot;Mastery&quot; &quot;Icy Chill of Despair&quot; &quot;Howl of the Banshee&quot; ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T16:35:34-08:00","id":1021744,"title":"","content":"I see no reason it would not, but the bonus would only apply when they were used against Garou. Of course, what is good for the goose is good for the gander, so beware of Black Spiral Dancers with Pure Breed 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T16:57:16-08:00","id":1021747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1021744#post1021744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason it would not, but the bonus would only apply when they were used against Garou. Of course, what is good for the goose is good for the gander, so beware of Black Spiral Dancers with Pure Breed 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yea, but I'd cry foul if I ran into a boat load of Pure Breed 5 White Howler BSD's.....it'd be a great &quot;big bad&quot; though that I'd encourage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T18:31:25-08:00","id":1021760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1021747#post1021747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well yea, but I'd cry foul if I ran into a boat load of Pure Breed 5 White Howler BSD's.....it'd be a great &quot;big bad&quot; though that I'd encourage.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm the last of the White Howlers!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, I'm the last of the White Howlers!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm the last of the White Howlers, and so is my wife!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T19:35:36-08:00","id":1021768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1021760#post1021760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I'm the last of the White Howlers!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, I'm the last of the White Howlers!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm the last of the White Howlers, and so is my wife!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Highlander<br /> Highlander II<br /> Highlander the Series","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T20:51:51-08:00","id":1021800,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that having PB 5 as a BSD does not make you a White Howler. It makes you a PB 5 BSD. The books have generally described the BSDs as being highly stratified with an elite of high PB characters, and a large number of low to no PB cannon fodder. So running into a pack of PB 4-5 BSDs is not actually implausible/a White Howler-fest. It's running into the Wyrm's equivalent of a Silver Pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T21:01:52-08:00","id":1021805,"title":"","content":"Implausible? Maybe not, but should it be just another Tuesday Night at Sunnydale? no....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T22:08:39-08:00","id":1021836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1021654#post1021654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Pure Breed is a physical thing that is often referred to as almost mystical (Revised, p. 122). The social dice pool bonus is one of the reasons why the Silver Fangs (which traditionally had to have three levels of Pure Breed) tended to rule the Garou Nation. I am curious though, would you say that the social dice pool bonus from Garou Pure Breed should apply to interactions with Garou Kinfolk? I would imagine that would allow Garou with high levels of Pure Breed to seduce Garou Kinfolk more easily, which would lead to greater reproductive success. In addition, it would seem that Garou Kinfolk receive their reproductive bonuses in addition to the social bonuses that they would receive when interacting with Garou (Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, p. 51).</div> </div> </div> </div>The social bonuses are never actually stated (or even mentioned) in K:UH. So it is entirely debatable on whether or not Kinfolk get them. The bonus for their Pure Breed, according to that book seems to be enhanced reproduction rates. Which is kind of in line with how the rest of the book treats them (as an extension of the Garou). Comparatively, Kinfolk: ABA doesn't mention Pure Breed in the kinfolk backgrounds section, but does mention it elsewhere in the book so they should still be able to take it in W20. Though there is zero mention of enhanced breeding rates, so who knows if that was meant to still be a thing.<br /> <br /> On whether or not a Garou's Pure Breed adds to rolls against Kinfolk? I say sure, why not. Garou aren't going to be in social contests against kinfolk much (generally speaking) and so extra bonus dice don't really bother me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1021673#post1021673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So quick Pure Breed question...that bonus applies to gifts that require a social die pool like &quot;Strength of Will&quot; or &quot;Mastery&quot; correct? I always played it that way because I never spotted a rule that said it didn't apply. Because if I've been playing it right, I think that helps highlight just how useful pure breed is to a Garou (especially considering the Garou unlike the other Fera have a relatively large number of fallen members to fight and use these dice pools in offensive gifts like &quot;Mastery&quot; &quot;Icy Chill of Despair&quot; &quot;Howl of the Banshee&quot; ).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is debatable, and I've seen it run both ways. This is how the line in W20 reads:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each point of Pure Breed adds an extra die to formal challenges (such as Rank challenges) and to Social rolls involving other Garou (even Ronin or Black Spiral Dancers). </div> </div> </div>I've generally considered Gift activation to be a separate thing than &quot;social rolls&quot;. I can absolutely see why it can (and possibly should) be read differently, but I personally feel that Pure Breed is powerful enough already, without enhancing Gift rolls as well.<br /> And the part about Rank Challenges bothers me in the new wording. Like, if you are in a combat challenge, what rolls does Pure Breed add to? If you are sent on a quest, do you add Pure Breed dice to everything along the way? Staredowns make sense. Gamecraft and combat does not imo. It hasn't come up for me yet, but I think if and when it does, I will go ahead and ignore that bit and just apply the dice to Staredowns only, like I've always done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:43:06-08:00","id":1024315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1019375-pure-breed-and-black-furies?p=1020765#post1020765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that relate to Pure Breed in Kinfolk though? Do Human Kinfolk lose their Pure Breed Background if they marry into another Tribe? Do Wolf Kinfolk lose their Pure Breed Background if they join a pack of another Tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess they loose it. Not that it matters much. Their trait is only for determining if kids bred true, iirc. No social bonuses like garou get...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}